  "chapter": 500,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 21 Chapter 500\n\n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8117, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the executive law, in relation to the processing\n        and maintenance of sexual offense evidence kits\"\n\n    APPROVED\n\n  This legislation would clear the backlog of  existing  sexual  offense\nevidence  kits  (Evidence  Kits),  mandate  the  timely  testing  of new\nEvidence Kits, and mandate information reporting related to the  ongoing\ntesting  of  Evidence Kits. This bill shines a light on, and attempts to\nresolve, a pressing concern. Survivors of sexual assault deserve to have\ntheir Evidence Kits processed in the fastest, and most effective  manner\npossible.\n\n  Unfortunately,  the  bill in its current form leaves open the opportu-\nnity for further harm to both survivors of sexual  assault  as  well  as\npolice  laboratories attempting to comply with the legislation's current\nmandates. The Executive has  secured  a  three-way  agreement  with  the\nLegislature  to  pass  legislation  in  the  upcoming session to correct\ndrafting errors and to ensure the proper and immediate auditing  of  all\nexisting Evidence Kits. On that basis, I am signing this bill.\n\n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2016
